    {
      "version": "1.14.0",
      "tag": "firmware-v1.14.0",
      "name": "firmware-v1.14.0",
      "date": "2026-11-17T00:42:29Z",
      "url": "https://github.com/fughilli/splanc/releases/tag/firmware-v1.14.0",
      "prerelease": false,
      "body": [
        {
          "t": "h2",
          "c": ["Highlights"]
        },
        {
          "t": "ul",
          "c": [
            {
              "t": "li",
              "c": [
                {
                  "t": "strong",
                  "c": ["Synced shows."]
                },
                " Uniform, effect, crossfade and brightness changes can carry an ",
                {
                  "t": "code",
                  "c": ["apply_at"]
                },
                " time so a room-wide change lands on the same frame on every fixture; the bridge keeps the shared time base disciplined, and stateful effects integrate on shared-time ",
                {
                  "t": "code",
                  "c": ["dt"]
                },
                " so they stay in step."
              ]
            },
            {
              "t": "li",
              "c": [
                {
                  "t": "strong",
                  "c": ["One colour-code kernel."]
                },
                " The mapping colour code (now hue code v2 with staggered cycles and a palette pilot) is a single Rust kernel shared by firmware, the web app (WASM) and Python tools."
              ]
            },
            {
              "t": "li",
              "c": [
                {
                  "t": "strong",
                  "c": ["ESP32-P4 support."]
                },
                " Splanc runs on the ESP32-P4 with a C6 front end and a wired Vive tracker, with one signed OTA package for both chips and DDP / Art-Net network outputs over Ethernet."
              ]
            },
            {
              "t": "li",
              "c": [
                {
                  "t": "strong",
                  "c": ["Wi-Fi connect fixes."]
                },
                " Busy vs. certificate errors are told apart, idle sessions hand over cleanly, an mbedTLS context overrun is fixed, and idle peers are reset before their slot is reclaimed (fixes Android ERR_TOO_MANY_RETRIES)."
              ]
            },
            {
              "t": "li",
              "c": [
                {
                  "t": "strong",
                  "c": ["Host player."]
                },
                " The Mac host player drives WLED over DDP / Art-Net with a shared time base and an output-latency offset."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
